# PAM service for nebula's login helper (nebula-login). Install as /etc/pam.d/nebula.
# Debian/Ubuntu layout; on other distributions mirror what /etc/pam.d/login (or sshd) uses. One PAM handle covers a
# whole sign-in: modules that need the password at session start (pam_mount, keyrings, systemd-homed) get it.
# PAM_RHOST is the browser's IP address (for pam_access, faillock and fail2ban); PAM_TTY is "nebula".
@include common-auth
@include common-account
@include common-session
